## Why This Is Asked

Tests a practical tenant-scoped access control pattern using existing CNF primitives (sidecars, Redis) without overengineering.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant identity via header
- Redis-backed authorization cache
- Safe proxying in a sidecar

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: sidecar filter
const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
const path = req.path;
redis.hget(`${tenant}:allowed`, path, (err, ok) => {
  if (!ok) res.status(403).send('forbidden');
  else forward(req);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you seed and rotate the allowlist safely?
- How to handle missing tenant or Redis latency?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design runtime policy reconfiguration with multi-tenant separation and zero-downtime updates.

## Key Concepts
- Central policy streaming via gRPC
- Per-tenant policy data model with versioning
- In-memory delta application with TTL and idempotence
- CRD design for policy declarations and rollout path

## Code Example
```proto
syntax = "proto3";
package policy;
message PolicyDelta {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string path_hash = 2;
  uint32 rate_limit = 3;
  uint32 window_seconds = 4;
  uint32 circuit_failure_limit = 5;
  uint32 circuit_reset_seconds = 6;
  uint32 log_sample_rate = 7;
  string policy_version = 8;
}
service PolicyService {
  rpc StreamPolicy(PolicyDelta) returns (stream PolicyDelta);
}
```

